From: =?UTF-8?q?Samuel=20Carre=C3=B1o?= <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:45:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g15: allow 8 prefixes in flight per VM (was 2),
 tunable with g15_max_inflight
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On the T6031 (J516C) a browser submits one render per job. With only two
prefixes in flight and ~612 us of host/firmware turnaround per flight while
the GPU work per render is ~88 us (asahi-g15/stats span vs busy), the engine
held publication on the in-flight cap ~3 times per job (stats hold[0]) and the
GPU idled ~85% of every flight: at 120 Hz Chrome's ~2.7k renders/s hit the
~3.3k/s ceiling and frames queued up as stutter. Power (17-24 W) and a
resolution-scaling test (1322 -> 1276 fps for 4x pixels) showed the GPU was
starved, not busy; pstate was already 8/8.

Raise FLIGHTS and MAX_INFLIGHT to 8 and add g15_max_inflight (0: tuned value,
1..8) so it can be lowered without a rebuild. Later flights still have to be of
the same VM; pass slots (16) and CT buffers bound the rest, and
publish_prefix_into already backs off with EAGAIN when they are held.

Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Samuel Carreño <soyminero11yt@gmail.com>
